# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) to configure `docker compose`. Everything here is optional: with no `.env` the demo runs
# with template-written drafts and no language model at all. A language model only ever WRITES the draft text; it never
# ranks, scores or decides anything, and every reply is checked against the facts before anyone sees it.

# The password every demo user shares (at least 12 characters). Give it to the reviewer in your message, not in git.
# PULSE_DEMO_PASSWORD=choose-a-long-passphrase

# ---- Drafting with a language model: pick ONE block, uncomment it ------------------------------------------------------

# A) Free and local: Ollama on your own machine. No key, no cost, nothing leaves the machine.
#    brew install ollama && ollama pull qwen2.5:7b && OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0 ollama serve
# PULSE_LLM_ENABLED=true
# PULSE_LLM_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# PULSE_LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# PULSE_LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b

# B) Free and hosted: Groq (a free key from console.groq.com; check its current free limits). Larger model, better prose.
# PULSE_LLM_ENABLED=true
# PULSE_LLM_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# PULSE_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# PULSE_LLM_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.8-27b
# PULSE_LLM_API_KEY=<your free Groq key>

# C) Anthropic Claude, when you have an API key. Nothing else changes.
# PULSE_LLM_ENABLED=true
# PULSE_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# PULSE_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# PULSE_LLM_API_KEY=<your Anthropic key>

# Check any block with ONE real call before a cycle:  docker compose run --rm api python3 -m pulse.cli llm-check
#   (prints the model, the latency and the rate limits the provider actually reported)

# ---- Real outbound email (leave unset for demo mode, where nothing is delivered to a customer) -------------------------
# PULSE_SMTP_HOST=
# PULSE_SMTP_PORT=587
# PULSE_SMTP_USER=
# PULSE_SMTP_PASSWORD=
